Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Round-wire analytical calibration", "Title",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"d13e7b8b-e6cf-9f4d-8ab0-a81f35eedd8f"],

Cell["\:7f2a\:96e8\:8f69 / Miao Yuxuan \[CenterDot] \:6dee\:5357\:5e08\:8303\
\:5b66\:9662 / Huainan Normal University", "Subtitle",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"489a6810-4adc-824f-815a-1677d4c41a60"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Model, inputs and scope", "Section",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"01ab11a6-75a3-7b49-b606-9a88b572a705"],

Cell["\[Del]\.b2Ez\[Minus]j\[Omega]\[Mu]\[Sigma]Ez=0; Zint=\[Kappa] I0(\
\[Kappa]a)/(2\[Pi]a\[Sigma] I1(\[Kappa]a))", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"b936aae8-2ab9-fa4e-ba33-54010f11a757"],

Cell["SI; exp(+j omega t); RMS; sigma=58 MS/m; mu_r=1; 20 C", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"589b9d1b-9b4e-4048-8a77-60d15d5d9fc0"],

Cell["\<\
Change frequency/current; compare independent current and Joule integrals.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"0ab14286-ad32-fc4a-83d9-88683b5016c1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Derivation and interpretation", "Section",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"9a49f908-db40-8447-8393-2ee864247331"],

Cell["\<\
For a homogeneous, long cylindrical conductor, symmetry leaves Ez(r) and Jz=\
\[Sigma]Ez. Combining Amp\[EGrave]re and Faraday laws with exp(+j\[Omega]t) \
gives (1/r)d(r dEz/dr)/dr=j\[Omega]\[Mu]\[Sigma]Ez. The regular solution is C \
I0(\[Kappa]r), \[Kappa]\.b2=j\[Omega]\[Mu]\[Sigma].\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"0732ccb6-e87c-6b4a-9a5b-1b3a74fa1528"],

Cell["\<\
Normalize C using 2\[Pi]\[Integral]Jz r dr=It. The terminal voltage gradient \
gives Zint=\[Kappa] I0(\[Kappa]a)/(2\[Pi]a\[Sigma] I1(\[Kappa]a)). \
Independently integrate \[Integral]|J|\.b2/\[Sigma] dA and compare with |It|\
\.b2 Re Zint. RMS phasors introduce no extra factor 1/2.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"4e7c6d83-c59f-7e4c-bcfc-427a2d4a57f5"],

Cell["\<\
As \[Kappa]a\[RightArrow]0, I0\[RightArrow]1 and I1\[RightArrow]\[Kappa]a/2, \
giving Rdc=1/(\[Sigma]\[Pi]a\.b2). The model excludes end effects and \
return-path external inductance. Q1 uses a=1 mm and remains a calibration \
case.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"30e6f34d-fbc8-ef44-ac31-bca06b96ac48"],

